From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:12:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: add T8132 (M4 Air, J713) support

Bind the sleep controller on apple,t8132-sleep with per-SoC match data:
register list, power word tables, wake names, displays, coprocessor
gates, CPU start bits, the PMU boot stage register and the last mile.

T8132 gets its own commit, in the order macOS uses in a sleep traced
under aura's hypervisor: other cores stopped, ATC0 and ANS/APCIE lowered,
WD2 armed, AMCC plane enables stepped off with bit 8 first, both memory
channels' lane enables down, the first channel's +0x588 word, each
plane's +0x4800 stage word, power gates with the fourth voter zeroed
before the third pass, clusters off, the XNU quiesce power-word reads,
clock muxes, then the commit. macOS then sends the PMU a few commands
before the boot core's deep WFI (0x2008 rewritten, 0x200e <- 0, 0x2000
<- 0x41); sleep and wake work without them, so they are left out.

T8132's CPU start bits are E at 0-5 and P from bit 6 (macOS writes
0x80/0x100/0x200 for its P cores), unlike T8140's 4*cluster+core.

T8132 sleeps are refused until the AIC's per-IRQ save is enabled for
its compatible (only apple,t8140-aic3 today) and ANS's APCIE tunables
are in the device tree; G16 and display coprocessors still running are
refused too. T8140 behaviour is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit a19cadb37ecf82175fd95ec468ff09deac04838f)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
